<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 14:18:12 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>Israeli strikes on southern Lebanon kill 11</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-israeli-strikes-on-southern-lebanon-kill-11</link><description>
Israeli strikes ⁠on a ​southern Lebanese town early on Monday killed at least 11 people including two children ​and two medics, Lebanon's state news agency said. Israel has intensified its bombardment of south Lebanon in recent days despite a June ceasefire that was meant ​to halt fighting ‌between the Israeli military and Lebanese armed ⁠group Hezbollah. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6c410c12-aac3-11f1-ba63-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/minilebanon.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6c410c12-aac3-11f1-ba63-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/minilebanon.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">76dbfbfa-aac3-11f1-b3a5-39bbc4f04cbf</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 14:10:28 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>arts24</category><title>Céline Dion and Jay-Z bring their hits to Paris</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260907-c%C3%A9line-dion-and-jay-z-bring-their-hits-to-paris</link><description>
In this edition of our arts24 music show, Jennifer Ben Brahim brings us a roundup of some of the week's most anticipated Paris concerts. From Céline Dion kicking off her 16 sold-out shows at La Défense Arena, to American rapper Jay-Z celebrating his 30-year career at the Stade de France, we've got you covered. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3c2fbf84-aabc-11f1-8cbe-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-16249183416a9eb5a6428b35-31705991.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3c2fbf84-aabc-11f1-8cbe-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-16249183416a9eb5a6428b35-31705991.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4c584f06-aabd-11f1-98ec-e7288cd5752f</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 14:05:13 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Jennifer BEN BRAHIM</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>What now for Germany's Merz after AfD win?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-what-now-for-germany-s-merz-after-afd-win</link><description>
The far-right AfD's triumph in the eastern state of Saxony-Anhalt marks a defeat for German Chancellor Friedrich Merz and sends a warning to other European leaders battling the same mixture of slow growth and disillusion with mainstream politics. In an increasingly polarized political system, Merz, whose personal approval ratings have sunk ‌to record lows, was one of the main targets of voter ire over the cost of living, pensions and economic insecurity. France 24’s Philip Turle takes a look at what the AfD’s victory means for the German leader and for Europe.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/89602e84-aac0-11f1-96ff-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-143117-143538-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/89602e84-aac0-11f1-96ff-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-143117-143538-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8eaab314-aac0-11f1-b490-39bbc4f04cbf</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 14:01:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Saxony-Anhalt poll: 'A huge blow for the CDU, but also a huge win for the AfD'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-saxony-anhalt-poll-a-huge-blow-for-the-cdu-but-also-a-huge-win-for-the-afd-1</link><description>
Carys Garland is pleased to welcome Markus Ziener, Visiting Senior Fellow at the German Marshall Fund. He interprets the AfD’s breakthrough in Saxony-Anhalt as a potentially historic turning point in post-war German politics. For Ziener, the significance lies not only in the scale of the far right’s electoral success, but also in the constituency behind it: many AfD voters, he argues, were previously politically disengaged rather than simply defecting from established parties. This complicates conventional explanations of the result as a straightforward transfer of support from the CDU to the AfD and raises a deeper question about the political expectations of a newly mobilised electorate.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3a1ef7e-aac2-11f1-ad2d-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-150057-150748-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3a1ef7e-aac2-11f1-ad2d-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-150057-150748-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a99d2b1e-aac2-11f1-b13f-39bbc4f04cbf</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 14:01:16 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>How far-right AfD breakthrough may ‘cause absolute chaos’ in Germany</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-how-far-right-breakthrough-may-cause-absolute-chaos-in-germany-afd</link><description>
Germany’s Alternative for Germany (AfD) came out well ahead in Sunday’s regional elections in the state of Saxony-Anhalt, becoming the first far-right party to come close to gaining power at the regional level since World War II. The lead candidate of the party in the state, Ulrich Siegmund, said Monday that his party had already initiated talks towards building a governing majority.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/99c5cf00-aa83-11f1-809d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26249706755348.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/99c5cf00-aa83-11f1-809d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26249706755348.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d78d6c00-aab8-11f1-8074-bb94302a716d</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 13:45:21 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/99c5cf00-aa83-11f1-809d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26249706755348.jpg">© Matthias Schrader, AP</source><dc:creator>Simon FEISTHAUER FOURNET</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Two children among dead in Israeli strikes on Lebanon</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-two-children-among-dead-in-israeli-strikes-on-lebanon</link><description>
Israeli airstrikes overnight killed 11 people in a south Lebanon village, including two infants, Lebanese state media said Monday, a day after separate raids left seven dead. France 24's Renée Davis in Beirut has the latest.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9d5282ce-aabc-11f1-a75a-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-140744-141004-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9d5282ce-aabc-11f1-a75a-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-140744-141004-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a1d61ec8-aabc-11f1-86b4-e7288cd5752f</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 13:20:18 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>REPLAY: 'Shocked' Merz speaks after far-right election victory</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-replay-shocked-merz-speaks-after-far-right-election-victory</link><description>
German Chancellor Friedrich Merz said Monday he was "deeply shocked" after his centre-right party suffered a heavy loss in a state poll to the far-right AfD, but vowed to push on with reforms. Watch his press conference in full above.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/054a05d8-aabc-11f1-a1f6-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-133511-135547-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/054a05d8-aabc-11f1-a1f6-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-133511-135547-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0a7c5286-aabc-11f1-95f3-e7288cd5752f</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 13:04:47 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>‘Idiots and traitors’: World reacts to AfD’s election victory</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-idiots-and-traitors-world-reacts-to-afd-s-election-victory</link><description>
The Alternative for Germany (AfD) surged into first place in state elections in Saxony-Anhalt on Sunday. The result puts a far-right party within reach of power at the state level for the first time in the country since World War II. The outcome has European capitals taking notice, particularly in France where the campaign for next year's presidential elections has gotten underway.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1ddd35d8-aab8-11f1-8553-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-120611-120807-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1ddd35d8-aab8-11f1-8553-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-120611-120807-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2272b848-aab8-11f1-98e4-bb94302a716d</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 13:02:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>UN rapporteur says Israeli rubble-clearing in Gaza could erase 'atrocity crimes' evidence</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260907-un-rapporteur-says-israeli-rubble-clearing-in-gaza-could-erase-atrocity-crimes-evidence</link><description>
The United Nations special rapporteur on Palestinian territories Francesca Albanese warned Monday that large-scale rubble removal in parts of Gaza under Israeli control could risk erasing "evidence relevant to the investigation of alleged international crimes". Israel's bombardment and ground offensive on Gaza has killed more than 73,000 Palestinians, according to Gaza's health ministry.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/22ab0c38-aac3-11f1-8592-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26236599212384.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/22ab0c38-aac3-11f1-8592-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26236599212384.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d529b836-aaba-11f1-8535-e7288cd5752f</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 12:51:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/22ab0c38-aac3-11f1-8592-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26236599212384.jpg">© Jehad Alshrafi, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'We’re all in crisis': Populist far-right 'trend' sweeping across Europe</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-we-re-all-in-crisis-populist-far-right-trend-sweeping-across-europe-1</link><description>
Annette Young is pleased to welcome our international affairs editor, Philip Turle, and Sylvie Bermann, France's first female ambassador to three member countries of the United Nations Security Council: China, the United Kingdom and Russia. The AfD’s breakthrough in Saxony-Anhalt should be understood, according to Sylvie Bermann, as part of a wider transformation of European politics rather than as an isolated German electoral shock. Brexit and Donald Trump’s victories helped normalise political positions previously regarded as outside the governing mainstream, while successive economic and geopolitical crises have weakened confidence in established parties. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2d5e75d2-aab6-11f1-bc26-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-130059-131732-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2d5e75d2-aab6-11f1-bc26-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-130059-131732-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">33b23d92-aab6-11f1-9063-ff9d54eec782</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 12:41:06 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Tech 24</category><title>Driverless taxi services are rolling out fast across the world</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/tech-24/20260907-driverless-taxi-services-are-rolling-out-fast-across-the-world</link><description>
From Austin to London, the current robotaxi boom is raising hard questions about safety and jobs. We take a closer look in this edition of Tech 24.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1903060c-aab6-11f1-aab3-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-6702827096a9eab5a21bcf2-98330213.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1903060c-aab6-11f1-aab3-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-6702827096a9eab5a21bcf2-98330213.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">52170c8e-a9f5-11f1-9e31-9b447c8e7aa4</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 12:29:33 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Charlotte Lam</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Who could form a coalition with Germany's AfD after election victory?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-who-could-form-a-coalition-with-germany-s-afd-after-election-victory</link><description>
Germany's far-right AfD won a landslide victory in a key regional election Sunday in the ex-communist east, a result seen as a stinging rebuke for Chancellor Friedrich Merz, but looked set to miss out on an absolute majority to govern alone. The big question now is who, if anyone, will be willing to form a coalition with the party, says France 24's correspondent Nick Holdsworth.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9b084944-aaa9-11f1-9300-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-120156-120548-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9b084944-aaa9-11f1-9300-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-120156-120548-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a00a1760-aaa9-11f1-b7c0-11268430d064</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 12:23:19 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French wine yields drop to new historic low after searing summer heat</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260907-scorching-summer-pushes-french-wine-harvest-to-new-historic-low</link><description>
French wine production is expected to suffer its worst harvest in some 70 years with the agriculture ministry on Monday forecasting a 6 percent drop in output after a summer of scorching temperatures, heatwaves and drought. France last week announced more than €1 billion in emergency support for farmers.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/45a0454c-aab3-11f1-8ad4-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/f0e62229cbdd19e6bec50a391c5d77395a3a4af6.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/45a0454c-aab3-11f1-8ad4-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/f0e62229cbdd19e6bec50a391c5d77395a3a4af6.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4694cc16-aab3-11f1-81c9-ff9d54eec782</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 11:57:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/45a0454c-aab3-11f1-8ad4-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/f0e62229cbdd19e6bec50a391c5d77395a3a4af6.jpg">© Sebastien Salom-Gomis, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Five dead after Amazon cargo plane overshoots runway in Miami</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-five-dead-after-amazon-cargo-plane-overshoots-runway-in-miami</link><description>
At least five people died when an Amazon Prime Air cargo flight overran a runway and crashed while landing at Miami International ​Airport on Sunday, local ‌officials said.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/87fb9dd8-aaa9-11f1-b952-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/miniplane-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/87fb9dd8-aaa9-11f1-b952-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/miniplane-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ad8586a4-aaa9-11f1-995a-01b725ef7820</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 10:54:03 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Lebanon president calls for US help after deadly Israeli strikes</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-lebanon-president-calls-for-us-help-after-deadly-israeli-strikes</link><description>
Lebanese President Joseph Aoun has urged Washington and the international community to help stop Israeli attacks, with strikes on the south of the country killing at least 11 people on Sunday despite a truce and a framework deal aimed at halting the violence.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d92f0c26-aaa4-11f1-94d1-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-103843-104014-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d92f0c26-aaa4-11f1-94d1-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-103843-104014-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ddfe9334-aaa4-11f1-8734-fdc7e1e88e57</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 10:21:29 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Segregated schools and citizen ‘watch groups’: the AfD’s plans for Saxony-Anhalt</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-segregated-schools-and-citizen-watch-groups-the-afd-s-plans-for-saxony-anhalt</link><description>
The Alternative for Germany (AfD) surged into first place in state elections in Saxony-Anhalt on Sunday, exit polls showed, putting a far-right party within reach of power at the state level for the first time since World War Two. So who are the AfD, and what could it mean for voters in the state? Rachael Griffiths has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f9865086-aaa1-11f1-ad15-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-103425-103610-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f9865086-aaa1-11f1-ad15-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-103425-103610-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fef7ba14-aaa1-11f1-8dfe-db5c2cd6173a</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 10:13:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Press Review</category><title>'Jubilation and pain': German far right marches to victory in key state election</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260907-jubilation-and-pain-german-far-right-marches-to-victory-in-key-state-election</link><description>
PRESS REVIEW – Monday, September 7: The far right marches to victory in a German state election: what does this mean for the future of Germany and Europe at large? Also: the Daily Telegraph publishes an exclusive interview with the sons of former Pakistani PM Imran Khan about his imprisonment conditions in Pakistan. Plus the US Open descends into chaos after influencers, weed and disruptions stir controversy.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/66bad82a-aaa2-11f1-ae88-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-3818120436a9e8a4e715ec8-42611865.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/66bad82a-aaa2-11f1-ae88-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-3818120436a9e8a4e715ec8-42611865.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">78efaf8e-aa84-11f1-a013-23a43548d837</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 10:05:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Dheepthika LAURENT</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title><![CDATA[Jamaica’s legal approach: Were forced transportation & African enslavement lawful under English law?]]></title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-jamaica-s-legal-approach-were-forced-transportation-african-enslavement-lawful-under-english-law</link><description>
Eve Irvine is pleased to welcome Jamaica’s Minister of Culture, Gender, Entertainment and Sport, Olivia Grange. According to Grange, the country’s reparations initiative attempts to shift the debate over British slavery from the terrain of political discretion to that of legal accountability. Was the capture, transportation and chattel enslavement of Africans in Jamaica ever lawful? Jamaica’s petition therefore asks King Charles III, in his capacity as King of Jamaica, to refer three questions to the Privy Council concerning English law, international law and Britain’s possible obligation to provide a reparatory remedy.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/190e7b02-aa9f-11f1-90f5-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-082047-082728-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/190e7b02-aa9f-11f1-90f5-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-082047-082728-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1dd8c3e0-aa9f-11f1-92a3-db5c2cd6173a</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 10:03:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Far-right AfD wins crushing victory in German state election</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-far-right-afd-wins-crushing-victory-in-german-state-election</link><description>
The far-right Alternative for Germany (AfD) surged into first place in state elections in Saxony-Anhalt on Sunday, exit polls showed, putting it within reach of power at the state level for the first time since World War Two, though falling just short of an overall majority.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/02f626c0-aaa0-11f1-9bcb-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-103216-103406-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/02f626c0-aaa0-11f1-9bcb-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-103216-103406-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">08054970-aaa0-11f1-b420-db5c2cd6173a</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 09:55:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Why are tourists flocking to French pharmacies?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-why-are-tourists-flocking-to-french-pharmacies</link><description>
After visiting the monuments and department stores, for some tourists in France, it’s off to the pharmacy. More and more foreign tourists are taking advantage of their stay to stock up on cosmetic products, sold in many pharmacies in France, which are known to be less expensive and very popular on social media.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/48a1d30a-aa9f-11f1-b194-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-102251-102455-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/48a1d30a-aa9f-11f1-b194-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-102251-102455-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4d3d0e66-aa9f-11f1-94ba-db5c2cd6173a</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 09:44:06 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>German startup carries out Europe's first commercial space launch</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-german-startup-carries-out-europe-s-first-commercial-space-launch</link><description>
German startup Isar Aerospace successfully launched its Spectrum rocket into orbit from Norway on Saturday night, marking the first ever such launch by a commercial entity from European soil. European firms are racing to make up ground in the lucrative launch industry, currently dominated by America's SpaceX.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e6f8bc5a-aa9d-11f1-96ed-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-102038-102208-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e6f8bc5a-aa9d-11f1-96ed-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-102038-102208-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">eba83a82-aa9d-11f1-ab50-db5c2cd6173a</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 09:41:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Business</category><title>German startup notches Europe's first successful private orbital launch</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20260907-german-startup-notches-europe-s-first-successful-private-orbital-launch</link><description>
German startup Isar Aerospace becomes the first company to achieve a successful private orbital space launch. But first: Germany's far-right AfD party scores a big electoral victory, pushed along in part by the country's structural economic crisis and its fiscal policies.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fd6e9158-aa98-11f1-9978-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/070926-BUSINESS-DAILY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fd6e9158-aa98-11f1-9978-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/070926-BUSINESS-DAILY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5eb99626-aa97-11f1-b6e7-9365a386766e</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 09:32:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Bryan QUINN</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nepal holds a day of mourning as rescuers continue search for flood missing</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-nepal-holds-a-day-of-mourning-as-rescuers-continue-search-for-flood-missing</link><description>
Grief-stricken Nepalis entered the traditional Hindu last day of mourning on Monday for the hundreds who died in the catastrophic flood along the country's border with China even as the government kept search operations going ​after four ‌miracle rescues in recent days.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/14af92fc-aa9b-11f1-a1db-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-101611-101754-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/14af92fc-aa9b-11f1-a1db-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-101611-101754-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">19de9f84-aa9b-11f1-a629-09ba76d48ded</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 09:25:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Germany seeks to dismiss Nicaragua's Gaza genocide case at top UN court</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-germany-seeks-dismissal-of-nicaragua-s-gaza-genocide-case-at-top-un-court</link><description>
Germany is set to ask the International Court of Justice on Monday to dismiss a case accusing Berlin of "facilitating genocide" in Gaza by supporting Israel after the deadly October 7, 2023 attacks by Hamas militants. The details of the case, filed by Nicaragua in 2024, have not yet been made public.
